+In this section, we explain the numerical methods used to approximately solve $(\mathbf{P})$ in the headline shaped specification and $(\bar{\mathbf{P}}_\lambda)$ in the shaping-off treatment.
+
+\paragraph{Numerical conditioning and replay.}
+We retain the common 18-coordinate observation. Before fitting training-only
+normalization statistics, we replace $H$ by $H-S^{\mathrm{mid}}$ and each
+slope-weighted quote $W$ by $W-S^{\mathrm{mid}}G$, retaining the original
+midprice and slopes. These are deterministic changes of coordinates. The
+normalizer uses 16 training paths spanning cancellation, persistent schedules,
+no-order auction behavior and large opening inventory, and is frozen thereafter.
+After initial-inventory centering, let $r_i$ denote the complete immediate
+reward, including the terminal component on the final step. Replay uses
+$\widetilde r_i=r_i+\Phi(y_{i+1})-\Phi(y_i)$, with
+$\Phi(\mathrm{terminal})=0$. During the CLOB phase,
+$\Phi(y)=(S^{\mathrm{mid}}-S_0^{\mathrm{mid}})I$.
+During the auction, write $G_a,W_a,G_e,W_e$ for the observed own and exogenous
+slope and slope-weighted-quote sums and $D$ for observed buy-minus-sell taker
+volume. Set
+\[
+\Delta=\frac{W_a-S^{\mathrm{mid}}G_a+W_e-S^{\mathrm{mid}}G_e+D}{G_a+G_e},
+\qquad \widehat Z=G_a\Delta-(W_a-S^{\mathrm{mid}}G_a),
+\]
+and $\Phi(y)=(S^{\mathrm{mid}}-S_0^{\mathrm{mid}})I+
+\Delta\widehat Z-\lambda(I-\widehat Z)^2$.
+This observable continuous-root estimate is a control variate; settlement still
+uses the actual tick-price pro-rata allocation. The potential telescopes, so
+it leaves the complete shaped return unchanged when $\Phi(y_0)=0$.
+DQN uses five-step replay targets that stop accumulating at phase boundaries
+and terminal states; the three library methods retain one-step replay. The
+DQN targets use sampled behavior continuations, without importance-sampling
+correction; thus they are an off-policy approximation, not an exact policy
+evaluation identity. Replay scaling never enters reported PnL.
 
